  "slug": "diet-lipidomic-d7ce",
  "summary": "Single-nucleus RNA-seq of 1.1 million hypothalamic nuclei in AD-BXD mice reveals sex-biased, cell-type-specific amyloid responses linked to early non-cognitive…",
  "synthesis": "The dominant thread is diet-driven remodeling of lipid handling in the intestine and liver, resolved with lipidomic and multi-omic readouts. Postprandial mesenteric lymph lipidomics in wild-type and Dennd5b knockout mice shows Dennd5b is required for chylomicron lipid export, including ceramides. Canine liver organoid monolayers capture Western-diet-induced hepatic reprogramming across transcriptomic, lipidomic, and biogenic amine signatures. Maternal high-fat diet in rats reduces tight junction organization, colonic SCFAs, and intestinal satiety peptides, linking perinatal inflammation to gut-brain signaling. A mathematical model connects meal-level appetite-driven food intake to metabolic changes under diets and semaglutide or exenatide treatment in mice. Separately, pregnancy-driven estradiol signaling expands intestinal Tregs that secrete IL-10 to drive small intestine remodeling. What is new is the joint use of lipid export genetics, organoid lipidomics, and feeding models to connect diet to systemic metabolic outcomes.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-haiku-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-19"
}
